The attached image, Figure 5, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A dot plots and Panel B histogram show that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone is modestly taken up, its uptake is markedly increased when adsorbed to AF647-labeled Nano-11. The Nano-11-antigen complexes are efficiently phagocytized by dendritic cells, with both Nano-11 and OVA co-localizing within the cells. This indicates that Nano-11 improves the intracellular delivery of negatively charged protein antigens to dendritic cells, a critical step for an effective immune response, and supports its role as a vaccine adjuvant.